ADC interlock threshold of channel $(CH) over 100 ms, in mV. Default 100000.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="combo" version="2.0.0">
      <name>AW</name>
      <pv_name>$(P):CH$(CH):ADC_WARN_TH</pv_name>
      <x>915</x>
      <y>35</y>
      <width>145</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(P):CH$(CH):ADC_WARN_TH (ADC_ILK_WARN_TH_CH$(CH))

ADC warning level of channel $(CH), as a fraction of the interlock
thresholds of the same channel: 50% (0), 25% (1) or 12.5% (2), default
12.5%. Raises warn_signal_&lt;scale&gt; when exceeded; a warning is only an
indication, it does not trip the interlock.

Shared by all five time scales of this channel at once and written to
interlock_threshold.reg0.warning_thd_switch as soon as the selection
changes. The driver applies no range check, so only these three enum values
are meaningful.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
      <items>
        <item>50%</item>
        <item>25%</item>
        <item>12.5%</item>
      </items>
    </widget>
